  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to IDPs and Congolese Refugees in Tombura-Yambio Diocese new wave</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a follow-up to the Yambio IDP and refugee response project response funded by CAFOD to address the  needs of refugees and IDPs affected by the displacements of populations in various locations in Yambio County as a result of LRA activities . The project aims to support the  Diocese of Tambura-Yambio to provide humanitarian  assistance to refugee and IDP communities  affected by re-surgent LRA activities in Ezzo Payam and makpandu refugee camp to gain access to safe water, sanitation and hygiene education. It also includes a component supporting vulnerable households and individuals to acquire Posho mills that will be used as income generating projects and in the process help to help communities to mill food stuffs donated food such as maize and sorgum into forms that the communities can more readily prepare for their food needs.</narrative>
  </description>
